        "compile_static": false,
        "code": "\n// update_record_by_id with useRawPayload REPLACES the record's properties - it does\n// not merge. Sending only the changed fields wiped planId, and the plan then could\n// not be found by the key it is looked up by. So the existing property set is read\n// first and the changes are laid over it.\ndef cur = (rows == null || rows.isEmpty()) ? [:] : (rows[0].properties ?: [:])\ndef out = [:]\ncur.each { k, v -> out[k] = v }\nout['name'] = String.valueOf(nm)\nout['description'] = String.valueOf(desc)\nout['periodId'] = String.valueOf(per)\nout['status'] = String.valueOf(stat)\nout['creditRuleIds'] = crIds\nout['payoutRuleIds'] = prIds\nreturn [payload: out]\n",
